200,"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"deadline":1791441334,"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udfe1 Changes recommended\n\nApp-server metadata is incomplete, one test task misreports its configuration, and standalone library API wiring lacks coverage.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>5 open findings</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Add Servlet 3.0 test for setCaptureUserName](#discussion_r4214330251) \u00b7 New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Add Servlet 5.0 test for setCaptureUserName](#discussion_r4214330276) \u00b7 New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Include request-parameters setting in metadataConfig](#discussion_r4214330303) \u00b7 New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Add user.name setting metadata to all app-server modules](#discussion_r4214330332) \u00b7 New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Fix unresolved UserIncubatingAttributes Javadoc link](#discussion_r4214330356) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced\n\n---\n\nGive feedback about Copilot approvals in [this survey](https://survey.alchemer.com/s3/9011660/CCR-Public-Preview-Autoapprove-feedback-survey) to enter a drawing for a $150 gift card.","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5451050225","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5451050225},{"body":"[Testing] No Servlet 3.0 standalone-library test invokes `Experimental.setCaptureUserName`; the common extractor unit test and installed-agent tests bypass this static handoff. A regression in the newly documented library API could therefore pass all current tests. Add a library test that configures this setter and verifies a request principal is emitted as `user.name`.","comment_commit_id":"105f78e29324477f9fc82cf517f715ce6c4c823d","comment_id":4214330251,"key":"inline:4214330251","kind":"inline","line":55,"original_commit_id":"105f78e29324477f9fc82cf517f715ce6c4c823d","original_line":55,"path":"instrumentation/servlet/servlet-3.0/library/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/servlet/v3_0/ServletTelemetryBuilder.java","review_commit_id":"105f78e29324477f9fc82cf517f715ce6c4c823d","review_id":5451050225,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-08T03:39:01Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"59b6886821e3f4f71d5866b3fb880be01fae14ffa5755a90d251315e15da4fd1","id":4214330251,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-08T03:39:01Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86qLuLs"},{"body":"[Testing] No Servlet 5.0 standalone-library test invokes `Experimental.setCaptureUserName`; the common extractor unit test and installed-agent tests bypass this static handoff. A regression in the newly documented library API could therefore pass all current tests. Add a library test that configures this setter and verifies a request principal is emitted as `user.name`.","comment_commit_id":"105f78e29324477f9fc82cf517f715ce6c4c823d","comment_id":4214330276,"key":"inline:4214330276","kind":"inline","line":55,"original_commit_id":"105f78e29324477f9fc82cf517f715ce6c4c823d","original_line":55,"path":"instrumentation/servlet/servlet-5.0/library/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/servlet/v5_0/ServletTelemetryBuilder.java","review_commit_id":"105f78e29324477f9fc82cf517f715ce6c4c823d","review_id":5451050225,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-08T03:39:01Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"a00efdde48a8451f375de58cf0347113469c79fee834a3121facec893a46e4ca","id":4214330276,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-08T03:39:01Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86qLuL9"},{"body":"[Testing] `withType<Test>().configureEach` also applies `otel.instrumentation.servlet.experimental.request-parameters.included=test-*` to this new task, but `metadataConfig` reports only the user-name setting. Metadata collected from the task is therefore labeled with an incomplete JVM configuration. Include both active properties in `metadataConfig`.","comment_commit_id":"105f78e29324477f9fc82cf517f715ce6c4c823d","comment_id":4214330303,"key":"inline:4214330303","kind":"inline","line":44,"original_commit_id":"105f78e29324477f9fc82cf517f715ce6c4c823d","original_line":44,"path":"instrumentation/tomcat/tomcat-10.0/javaagent/build.gradle.kts","review_commit_id":"105f78e29324477f9fc82cf517f715ce6c4c823d","review_id":5451050225,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-08T03:39:01Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"8c48919e24f3be2a50c803ca31aef80f1e3cde93a5e8ff233f03f72fab91e2f5","id":4214330303,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-08T03:39:01Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86qLuMM"},{"body":"[Config] The new shared setting is only referenced by the Servlet and Spring Security metadata, but it is also read for app-server-owned spans through `AgentServletInstrumenterBuilder` and `BaseServletHelper` (including Tomcat, Jetty, Liberty, Grizzly, and Undertow). Those modules can emit `user.name` while their generated settings documentation omits the property; the new Tomcat test demonstrates this mismatch directly. Add `common.user.name.enabled` refs to every affected app-server module's `metadata.yaml`.","comment_commit_id":"105f78e29324477f9fc82cf517f715ce6c4c823d","comment_id":4214330332,"key":"inline:4214330332","kind":"inline","line":209,"original_commit_id":"105f78e29324477f9fc82cf517f715ce6c4c